build: 2026-06-21 v10.34.30 (AUv3 host — insert an effect on the plugin channel)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
includes: Echoel now hosts AUv3 EFFECTS, not just instruments. In Tools ▸ Plugins, tap an effect and it inserts on the hosted instrument's channel — instrument → effect → master, the Ableton device-chain idea. The loaded bar shows the instrument with a "→ effect" line and a Remove button; instruments still play from the preview keyboard or your song. The effect only processes the hosted plugin (it stays off Echoel's own mix path, so it's safe and contained); an effect with no instrument loaded waits unconnected until you add one. Built on new audio-engine chain primitives (pause/attach/connect/restart, the same safe path Echoel's voices use) with one canonical stereo format so mono/stereo plugins don't mismatch. Audio-thread reviewed clean. Next in the arc: showing a plugin's own interface, saving plugin state, and a master-bus effect slot. Verified: Xcode Compile Check + CI green.
